{
  "note": "Derived by hand from data/pages/IAM__latest__UserGuide__reference_aws-services-that-work-with-iam.md with a standalone script that re-reads the raw table, independently of the parser. The table has 440 data rows (lines 24-463) and 7 columns. Column 1 is the service name; columns 2-7 are the six IAM capabilities, each Yes, No or Partial \u2014 every one of the 2640 verdict cells reads as exactly one of those three, so no row was skipped for an unreadable cell. There is no More information column in the table, so no feature is made for one. Each capability column is one feature: Yes is covered/full, Partial is covered/partial, No is excluded. Names were resolved with resolveService on the raw label, and, only when that failed and the label ends in a parenthetical (the AWS \"Full Name (Abbrev)\" form), on the long form alone. That parenthetical retry recovers 17 rows: ec2, ebs, ecr, ecr-public, ecs, elasticfilesystem, eks, kms, acm-pca, rds, ram, sts, sns, sqs, s3, swf and the Amazon VPC row. Nothing else was normalised, so a name AWS spells differently from services.json (for example \"AWS Elastic Load Balancing\" against \"Elastic Load Balancing\") stays unresolved rather than being guessed at. 288 of the 440 rows resolved; 152 did not and are recorded in unresolved, never counted. Four resolved rows repeat a service another row already represents. One id can carry one verdict, so the row that spells out the id represents it and the others are dropped whole: rds is Amazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS), not Amazon Neptune or Amazon Neptune Analytics; ec2 is Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2), not Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC); iot is AWS IoT, not AWS IoT Greengrass. 440 = 284 counted + 152 unresolved + 4 repeats. That leaves 284 distinct services, and every feature has covered + excluded = 284. Per column: Actions 283 Yes + 1 Partial + 0 No; Resource-level permissions 243 + 11 + 30; Resource-based policies 29 + 6 + 249; ABAC 206 + 17 + 61; Temporary credentials 277 + 4 + 3; Service-linked roles 110 + 9 + 165.",
